nts they  seem to be making is that he doesn't  have any money but his bond of 7 million  is so high  and this is someone i argue all the time  that bail should be lowered because  don't you can't judge someone's criminal  record it's will they come back to court  or not well this is a guy who literally  has unknown hidden assets that he stole  from clients has shown that he may  commit suicide or just up and leave i  think he's a high high high flight risk  so any bail reduction at all i think is  going to be minimal if any uh i think  there's no further more more poignant  arguments his defense attorneys can make  and i just don't see anything happening  that's going to get this guy out of jail  all right as the judge says they will be  giving a written order and when we get  that we'll make sure to give you the  update and this the murdoch murder  mystery coming up on law and crime daily  the jury hears experts testimony as  chandler halderson stands trial for the  murder of his parents plus accused  parkland school shooter nicholas cruz is  back in court why the prosecution  requests a delay only a month away from  his coming sentencing  [Music]  hi this is dan abrams with exciting news  for all of our law and crime followers  on youtube you can now get the live law  and crime network with youtube tv for  all of your daily live trial coverage  legal news expert analysis and original  true crime programs subscribe to youtube  tv today and then locate law and crime  in the channel guide and for only 1.99 a  month you can add the network to your  bundle  watch lawn crime every day with youtube  tv we put you in the jury bonus  [Music]  welcome back tuesday morning prosecutors  asked the judge to delay the penalty  phase again for nicholas cruz the man  responsible for killing 17 of his  classmates and teachers nearly four  years ago at a high school in parkland  florida on february 14 2018 cruz carried  out the deadliest school shooting in the  country when he opened fire on students  and staff at marjory stoneman douglas  high school 17 people died and 17 others  were injured this past october crews  pled guilty to 17 counts of first degree  murder and 17 counts of attempted murder  cruz's penalty phase is set to begin  february 21st his defensive team once  again said at a hearing tuesday morning  that they will be filing a motion to  remove the death penalty from the table  at that hearing prosecutors said they  won't be ready for sentencing saying  that they haven't received enough  information from experts who are  expected to testify  we've been ready every time on the gilt  phase uh we haven't received the  material we can't take their depositions  uh you know it's the first time we're  ever moving uh for a continuance  i don't see how we can be ready on the  21st and the defense and i understand  this they're still taking depositions of  our witnesses  well mr satz i don't intend on  continuing this case any further out uh  we just do jury selection those uh three  days a week so that you all have the  thursday and friday of those two weeks  in february that's fine  but if you think you can't be ready  because of something the defense is  doing or not doing then please file a  motion but i'm not continuing it any  longer  let's bring back criminal defense  attorney adam conte and co-host terry  austin to discuss cruz's sentence  terry why the rush why do you think the  judge isn't giving the lawyers more time  i love the judge's disposition here i  don't think she should give a  continuance listen like you said it's  been nearly four years since this mass  shooting and there have been delays  already because of covet they can't you  know the case has got to get moving  that's what the judge wants to do here  to see the penalty phase get started she  doesn't want to put over again any more  delays in this trial so you know the  other issue here brian is that these  families deserve justice it's you know  months since cruz has pled guilty and  his attorneys have had an opportunity to  prepare they know who the experts are  they can take these depositions and  there's plenty of time so i agree with  the judge i think she should just keep  this moving just to have some  consolation for the victim 17 killed and  17 injured  now out of how big of a sentencing  hearing do you think this will be what  do you expect with all of these  potential  experts yeah this is interesting to me  because all we're really talking about  here is the death penalty right this is  just a state  where a lot of people really love the  death penalty and some people don't  and so that's why you know why why  wouldn't this just be okay  life without parole  done deal you're gonna spend the rest of  your life in prison you have no chance  of ever seeing the light of day again  perhaps you'll go to a mental hospital  if you're cured from your mental defect  then you'll go to a regular maximum  security prison  i don't understand the point of what's  about to happen which i think is going  to be a very involved hearing with  experts talking about mental health and  effect on uh the effect on him and and  all these other outside factors it just  seems so simple to me and maybe i'm just  not looking at it at the at a in a  lawyerly way maybe i should be looking  at it like with through the eyes of an  attorney but just let's take common  sense for a minute put him in jail for  the rest of his life nobody has to  suffer anymore the judge can be done the  prosecutors can be done and we can all  go home and start moving on with our  lives i agree adam but that may be the  new york lawyers in in both of us and  agreeing there where florida as you said  operates a little differently but we'll  see as this sentencing phase continues  for nicolas cruz when we come back we  head to wisconsin where chandler  halderson stands trial for the murder  and dismemberment of his parents that  what damning evidence investigators  f